# Secrets — never commit. Only .env.example is tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime data
data/
media/
logs/

# Photographs of children. These arrive from the school as loose folders and land
# wherever they are unzipped -- which is how they end up NEXT TO the repo root rather
# than under media/, where the rules above would have caught them. Named explicitly,
# because `git add -A` does not ask twice and a push cannot be taken back.
student_photos/
original_student_photos/
*_student_photos/

# Evaluation footage. `eval/labels.csv` and `eval/baseline.json` are the *results* and
# belong in git; the clips they refer to are video of children and never do. Nor do the
# crop ROIs, nor the candidate/sample lists, whose every row names a child's clip.
eval/clips/
eval/crops/
eval/candidates.csv
eval/candidates.coverage.csv
eval/candidates.unreadable.csv
eval/sample.csv
# `eval scan` rewrites its artifacts after every clip, through a temp file renamed over the
# real one. A run killed inside a write leaves one behind, and it names clips too.
eval/*.partial

*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.db

# Model weights (fetched by scripts/fetch_models.py).
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and it must stay that way. An un-anchored `models/`
# matches a directory named `models` at ANY depth -- which silently excluded
# `src/qorgan/db/models/` (8 files: Person, Event, CanteenSession, auth...) and
# `src/qorgan/models/` (PersonDetector, PoseEstimator) from the repository entirely.
# Everything ran fine on the machine that had them on disk; a fresh clone could not
# import qorgan.db.models at all. The tests never caught it, because tests run against
# the disk, not against git.
/models/
*.pt
*.onnx

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Clips we could not attribute to a camera. Video of children; awaiting the school.
eval/unresolved/

# Loose folders of children that land beside the repo root because that is how the school
# sends them: an archive, unzipped where it was downloaded. Every one of these was found
# UNIGNORED and one frame from being pushed.
#
# `git check-ignore -q some_dir/` is NOT how you check this -- it answers about the
# directory and lied about all four of these. Ask about a FILE, or ask `git add -An` and
# read what it says it would add. That is the only check that has ever caught anything here.
#
# ANCHORED to the repo root with a leading slash, on purpose. An unanchored `faces/`
# matches ANY directory of that name -- including `src/qorgan/faces/` and
# `src/qorgan/canteen/`, the source packages. It did: a new file under either would have
# been silently ignored, and an agent had to `git add -f` to commit `faces/gallery.py`.
# The school dumps its archives at the ROOT, so anchor there and stop shadowing source.
/Bandicut/
/faces/
/crops/
/snapshots/
/bullying_camera/
/class/
# Added 2026-07-27, and it is the fifth time this comment block has been proved right:
# this delivery sat UNIGNORED for a day and `git add -An` listed 323 of its paths, 141 of
# them photographs of children. Only the OUTER directory name is clean UTF-8; the inner
# ones are UTF-8 bytes stored as CP866 (`1╨Р` is `1А`), so anchor on the outer name and
# verify with `git check-ignore -v` against a FILE inside, never against the directory.
# NOT quoted: .gitignore has no quoting, a `"` is a literal character. The quoted form was
# written first and `git add -An` still listed all 323 paths -- which is why that check is
# the one this block insists on.
/фотки учеников/

# The school's own labelling spreadsheet. Names of children against incidents, which is
# the most sensitive file they have sent yet.
*.xlsx

# Every archive: the school sends footage and class photos as .zip, unzipped where it
# lands. Naming each folder as it arrives is how we got to six rules and one near miss.
*.zip

# Any video, anywhere. The school sends canteen footage and screen recordings straight
# into the repo root, and naming each new folder was always going to lose the race. A
# screen recording of the dashboard shows children's faces on the recognition view.
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov
*.mkv
# Root-anchored: an unanchored `canteen/` shadowed the `src/qorgan/canteen/` package.
/canteen/

# ИСКЛЮЧЕНИЕ ДЛЯ ДАННЫХ СТЕНДА, и оно обязано быть ИМЕННО ЗДЕСЬ.
#
# Правила выше (`media/`, `data/`, `*.sqlite3`) запрещают базы и медиа во всём этом
# каталоге и остаются в силе. Исключение в КОРНЕВОМ .gitignore их не отменяет: для путей
# внутри `qorgan-ai-main/` главнее этот файл, и `git add` молча не видел ни одного кадра,
# хотя они лежали на диске.
#
# Порядок важен: сначала снимается запрет с самой папки, потом с её содержимого — git не
# заходит внутрь исключённого каталога и не может «спасти» файл, не вернув сперва каталог.
!seed/
!seed/**
